{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/SignalBatchStrategy","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/BatchStrategy","doc:\/\/Afluent\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Afluent\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To","kind":"relationships"}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/SignalBatchStrategy\/init(_:)"],"generated":true,"title":"Initializers","anchor":"Initializers"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/SignalBatchStrategy\/signal"],"generated":true,"title":"Instance Properties","anchor":"Instance-Properties"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/SignalBatchStrategy\/run(_:)"],"generated":true,"title":"Instance Methods","anchor":"Instance-Methods"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/SignalBatchStrategy\/BatchStrategy-Implementations"],"generated":true,"title":"Default Implementations","anchor":"Default-Implementations"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SignalBatchStrategy","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Element","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Signal","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Signal","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Sendable","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8SendableP"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Signal","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AsyncSequence","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sci"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The signal’s elements are ignored; only their arrival counts. Use it with a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/PassthroughSubject","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" or a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/CurrentValueSubject","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" to flush on demand. A value already"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"available at subscription, such as a "},{"code":"CurrentValueSubject","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"‘s current value, fires when the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"signal’s task subscribes. That task starts alongside the upstream’s, so elements may already"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"have arrived and the first batch may be short. A signal that finishes stops firing and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"batches go on until the upstream finishes; a signal that throws ends the batched sequence with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its error, except "},{"code":"CancellationError","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" while the batched sequence is still running (a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/SingleValueSubject","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" someone else cancelled): then the signal stops firing and the batches go"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Example","anchor":"Example","type":"heading"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let flush = PassthroughSubject<Void>()","for try await lines in logLines.batch(strategy: .signal(flush)) {","    write(lines)","}","\/\/ Elsewhere, when the app moves to the background:","flush.send()"],"type":"codeListing"}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/afluent\/signalbatchstrategy"]}],"s